 // after a direct al_response create, so save() could remember it for the next
 // PATCH. There is no create here any more - AnswerWriter finds or creates the
 // row server-side - so nothing on this page needs the id, and the function is
 // gone with the create it served.{% endcomment %}

 function two(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; }

 {% comment %}/*
 * CACHE_LAG. F5, found in DEV on 2026-09-20. An answer saves correctly, the page
 * says "Saved", and reloading within the next fifteen minutes can render the form
 * empty. The page reads al_response through Liquid; the write is made by
 * AnswerRequestPlugin as the application user; and a plug-in write never
 * invalidates the portal's data cache (AD-094). Nothing is lost - the rows are in
 * Dataverse, and the submit check reads them server-side, so a submit from a page
 * that looks empty still succeeds - but an empty form after a save reads as lost
 * work, and the first instinct is to type it all again.
 *
 * So the page remembers which answers it saved, for this review, in this tab, and
 * says so when the server has not caught up.
