 * Remedial action required? from the outcome, and saying when a stored
 * answer was cleared out from under the checker - are withdrawn (project
 * owner, 2026-10-05: "Remove any parts of the form that are automatically
 * greyed out or selected by default - leave them open, allow any answer").
 * The server accepts any answer since 2026-10-05 (AD-231); the page simply
 * draws every option open.
 */{% endcomment %}
 }
 })();
 </script>
 {% endif %}

 {% endif %}
 {% endif %}

 {% comment %}
 Remediation and escalation is NOT on this form.

 The document carries it as a closing block marked "(PICKED UP ON ANOTHER FORM)", and
 that is how it is built: al_RemediationAction, al_Signoff and al_Outcome, worked on the
 remediation page and the sign-off step, per case rather than per review (AD-095). This
 page used to render a read-only copy of it beneath the checklist; the project owner's
 direction on 2026-09-09 was that the checklist form is the checklist and remediation
 belongs to its own step, so the copy and its three fetches are gone. Nothing about the
 remediation data changed - only where it is read.
 {% endcomment %}

 {% comment %}
 Submit panel (PP-07, PP-11). Deliberately the last thing on the page.

 It used to sit directly under the summary card, above the questionnaire, so on a
 42-question checklist the button was off-screen by the time a reviewer had answered
 anything and submitting meant scrolling back up past every answer. Submitting is the
 end of the task, so it belongs at the end of the page - reached by finishing the
 questionnaire rather than by scrolling away from it.

 The button is only an affordance: the submission re-checks the transition, every
 mandatory question and the Tax-before-AQS rule server-side, so moving, hiding or
 showing it changes nothing about what is permitted (NFR-SEC-01).
 {% endcomment %}
 {% comment %}
 Who carries the fail (project owner, 2026-09-19), at the end of the check and before
 the Submit button, which is where the checker is when they know the answer.

 Only when this check has failed. Accountability describes a fail: on a clean check
 there is nobody to name, and the server refuses one anyway.

 The four flags live on al_outcome, and that row does not exist yet - SubmitReviewPlugin
 creates it when this review is submitted. So the choice is parked on the review and
 applied to the outcome the submit creates, in the same write as the grade.

 The people come from the contact directory, which checkers can now read: a global
 read-only table permission was added for it (Contact - directory read). They can see
 the directory and still write only their own row, which is the row the request below
 is PATCHed onto.
 {% endcomment %}
 {% if editable %}
 {% comment %}
 The opening state only, not the decision.

 This card is rendered on every editable review and hidden until the check records a
 non-pass; the script below shows and hides it as the answers change. It used to be
 wrapped in this condition instead, which meant the server decided at PAGE LOAD
 whether the card existed - so a checker who ticked Fail saw nothing, because ticking
 an answer autosaves and never re-renders the page. It appeared only after a reload.
 Reported on IO-SEED-TAX-01, 2026-09-19.

 The rule here and the rule in the script are the same one: any answer on the
 outcome scale that is not a plain Pass.
 {% endcomment %}
 {% assign ot_fq_failed = false %}
 {% for a in arows %}
 {% assign ot_ans = a.al_answerchoice.value %}
 {% if ot_ans == 120910301 or ot_ans == 120910302 or ot_ans == 120910303 or ot_ans == 120910304 %}
 {% assign ot_fq_failed = true %}
 {% endif %}
 {% endfor %}

 {% comment %}
 Every active contact, unfiltered on purpose. A pick is sent as the contact's id and the
 server takes any contact id (AccountabilityRequestPlugin.ParseOptionalContact); nothing
 downstream needs an email, so a contact without one is still a valid pick, and one
 already saved has to stay in this list or the next save would clear it (restoreSaved
 leaves the box blank for an id it cannot find). The count is the platform's largest
 page, stated so the list is never cut at a smaller default without anyone noticing.
 {% endcomment %}
 {% fetchxml directory %}
 <fetch count="5000">
 <entity name="contact">
 <attribute name="contactid" />
 <attribute name="fullname" />
 <attribute name="emailaddress1" />
 <filter type="and">
 <condition attribute="statecode" operator="eq" value="0" />
 </filter>
 <order attribute="fullname" />
 </entity>
 </fetch>
 {% endfetchxml %}

 <section class="ot-card ot-accountability"
 data-ot-accountability
 data-review-id="{{ rv.al_reviewinstanceid }}"
 data-ot-acc-saved="{{ rv.al_pendingaccountability | escape }}"
 {% unless ot_fq_failed %}hidden{% endunless %}
 aria-labelledby="ot-accountability-heading">
 <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-accountability-heading">Who carries this fail</h2>
 <p>
 This check records a fail. Say who carries it before you submit. Left alone, the
 extract names the people the case itself does: the paraplanner for a File Quality
 Fail, the adviser for Insufficient evidence or Potential harm. Nobody is named for
 any other grade.
 </p>

 <div class="ot-accountability__grid">
 <fieldset class="ot-accountability__set">
 <legend>File Quality</legend>
 <label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" data-ot-acc="fqParaplanner" /> The paraplanner ({{ rv['case.al_paraplanner'] | default: 'not named' | escape }})</label>
 <label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" data-ot-acc="fqAdviser" /> The adviser ({{ rv['case.al_advisername'] | default: 'not named' | escape }})</label>
 <label class="ot-accountability__person">
 <span>Or someone else</span>
 <input type="text" class="ot-hdr-input" list="ot-acc-people"
 data-ot-acc-person="fq" placeholder="Search for a person"
 autocomplete="off" role="combobox"
 aria-label="Person carrying the File Quality fail" />
 </label>
 </fieldset>

 <fieldset class="ot-accountability__set">
 <legend>Advice Quality</legend>
 <label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" data-ot-acc="aqAdviser" /> The adviser ({{ rv['case.al_advisername'] | default: 'not named' | escape }})</label>
 <label class="opt"><input type="checkbox" data-ot-acc="aqParaplanner" /> The paraplanner ({{ rv['case.al_paraplanner'] | default: 'not named' | escape }})</label>
 <label class="ot-accountability__person">
 <span>Or someone else</span>
 <input type="text" class="ot-hdr-input" list="ot-acc-people"
 data-ot-acc-person="aq" placeholder="Search for a person"
 autocomplete="off" role="combobox"
 aria-label="Person carrying the Advice Quality fail" />
 </label>
 </fieldset>
 </div>

 {% comment %}
 One datalist for both boxes: a datalist is a list of suggestions, not a control,
 so two inputs can point at the same one and it is rendered once rather than twice.

 The option's text is what someone types to choose a person, so it has to identify
 them on its own - name and email together, since two people can share a name. The
 contact's id rides on data-id, because a datalist yields TEXT and cannot carry a
 record; the script maps the text back.
 {% endcomment %}
 <datalist id="ot-acc-people">
 {% for c in directory.results.entities %}
 <option value="{{ c.fullname | escape }} - {{ c.emailaddress1 | escape }}" data-id="{{ c.contactid }}"></option>
 {% endfor %}
 </datalist>

 <p class="ot-accountability__status" data-ot-acc-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 </section>

 <script>
 (function () {
 'use strict';
 var root = document.querySelector('[data-ot-accountability]');
 if (!root) { return; }

 var status = root.querySelector('[data-ot-acc-status]');
 var reviewId = root.getAttribute('data-review-id');
 var boxes = root.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-acc]');
 var timer = null;
 var saving = false;
 {% comment %}// Something moved while a save was on its way. Every save sends the whole state, so
 // one more save when that one lands is all it takes (2026-09-24, the same fault the
 // case header had on 900000006).{% endcomment %}
 var saveAgain = false;

 function show(message, kind) {
 status.textContent = message;
 status.className = 'ot-accountability__status' + (kind ? ' ot-inline-status--' + kind : '');
 }

 {% comment %}/*
 * The box IS the search (project owner, 2026-09-19). A native datalist: the
 * browser filters as you type and owns the keyboard, the scrolling and the
 * screen-reader semantics, none of which a hand-rolled list gets right for free.
 *
 * What it costs is that it yields TEXT, not a record, so the text has to identify
 * one person on its own and be mapped back to an id. Anything that matches nobody
 * records nobody, and says so rather than failing at the server.
 */{% endcomment %}
 var byText = {};
 var options = document.querySelectorAll('#ot-acc-people option');
 for (var o = 0; o < options.length; o++) {
 byText[options[o].value.trim().toLowerCase()] = options[o].getAttribute('data-id');
 }

 function value(name) {
 var box = root.querySelector('[data-ot-acc="' + name + '"]');
 return box ? box.checked : false;
 }

 function person(which) {
 var box = root.querySelector('[data-ot-acc-person="' + which + '"]');
 if (!box) { return ''; }
 var typed = box.value.trim().toLowerCase();
 if (typed === '') { return ''; }
 return byText[typed] || '';
 }

 {% comment %}/** Names anyone the boxes hold text for but could not match. */{% endcomment %}
 function unmatched() {
 var stray = [];
 var which = ['fq', 'aq'];
 for (var i = 0; i < which.length; i++) {
 var box = root.querySelector('[data-ot-acc-person="' + which[i] + '"]');
 if (box && box.value.trim() !== '' && person(which[i]) === '') {
 stray.push(box.value.trim());
 }
 }
 return stray;
 }

 {% comment %}/** The section as it stands, in the shape a save sends and al_pendingaccountability keeps. */{% endcomment %}
 function currentState() {
 return {
 fqAdviser: value('fqAdviser'),
 fqParaplanner: value('fqParaplanner'),
 aqAdviser: value('aqAdviser'),
 aqParaplanner: value('aqParaplanner'),
 fqContactId: person('fq'),
 aqContactId: person('aq')
 };
 }

 {% comment %}/*
 * Draws the accountability this check already holds (2026-09-24). The page used to
 * draw four empty boxes and empty names on every visit, and because every save
 * carries the whole state, the first change after reopening saved that emptiness
 * over the checker's earlier choices. A saved person is named from the directory by
 * id; one no longer in it is left blank rather than guessed.
 */{% endcomment %}
 function restoreSaved() {
 var saved = null;
 try { saved = JSON.parse(root.getAttribute('data-ot-acc-saved') || 'null'); }
 catch (e) { saved = null; }
 if (!saved) { return; }

 for (var r = 0; r < boxes.length; r++) {
 boxes[r].checked = saved[boxes[r].getAttribute('data-ot-acc')] === true;
 }

 var sides = ['fq', 'aq'];
 for (var k = 0; k < sides.length; k++) {
 var id = saved[sides[k] + 'ContactId'];
 var input = root.querySelector('[data-ot-acc-person="' + sides[k] + '"]');
 if (!input || !id) { continue; }
 for (var o2 = 0; o2 < options.length; o2++) {
 if (options[o2].getAttribute('data-id') === id) { input.value = options[o2].value; break; }
 }
 }
 }

 {% comment %}/*
 * CACHE_LAG, as the header and the answers handle it. The save goes through a
 * plug-in, so the site's render cache learns of it late (AD-094: up to fifteen
 * minutes) and a reload inside that window draws the state from before the save.
 * The tab remembers what it saved and says so; it never re-applies it, because a
 * value on screen the server did not send cannot be told from one it did.
 */{% endcomment %}
 var ACC_LAG_KEY = 'ot.savedAccountability.' + reviewId;
 var ACC_LAG_WINDOW_MS = 20 * 60 * 1000;

 function readSavedAccountability() {
 try { return JSON.parse(window.sessionStorage.getItem(ACC_LAG_KEY) || 'null'); }
 catch (e) { return null; }
 }

 function writeSavedAccountability(saved) {
 {% comment %}// Private browsing and a full store both throw; the notice is a courtesy.{% endcomment %}
 try {
 if (saved === null) { window.sessionStorage.removeItem(ACC_LAG_KEY); }
 else { window.sessionStorage.setItem(ACC_LAG_KEY, JSON.stringify(saved)); }
 } catch (e) { {% comment %}/* no notice this time */{% endcomment %} }
 }

 function sameState(a, b) {
 var flags = ['fqAdviser', 'fqParaplanner', 'aqAdviser', 'aqParaplanner'];
 for (var f = 0; f < flags.length; f++) {
 if ((a[flags[f]] === true) !== (b[flags[f]] === true)) { return false; }
 }
 return (a.fqContactId || '') === (b.fqContactId || '')
 && (a.aqContactId || '') === (b.aqContactId || '');
 }

 function reportAccountabilityLag() {
 var saved = readSavedAccountability();
 if (!saved || !saved.state) { return; }
 if (Date.now() - saved.at > ACC_LAG_WINDOW_MS || sameState(saved.state, currentState())) {
 writeSavedAccountability(null);
 return;
 }
 show('Who carries this fail is not shown here yet. Your last change was saved. This'
 + ' site caches pages for up to fifteen minutes, so a reload can arrive before the'
 + ' page catches up. Do not change it again yet — reload in a few minutes, or'
 + ' the next change would save what is on screen over it.', 'error');
 }

 function save() {
 if (timer) { window.clearTimeout(timer); timer = null; }
 if (saving) { saveAgain = true; return; }
 if (!window.shell || typeof window.shell.getTokenDeferred !== 'function') {
 show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
 return;
 }

 var stray = unmatched();
 if (stray.length > 0) {
 show('Nobody in the directory matches "' + stray[0] + '", so nobody was'
 + ' recorded for it. Pick a name from the list.', 'error');
 return;
 }

 saving = true;
 show('Saving...', null);

 {% comment %}// What this save sends, kept so a reload inside the cache window can be told apart
 // from one that has caught up (reportAccountabilityLag).{% endcomment %}
 var sent = currentState();
 var body = {
 al_accountabilityrequest: JSON.stringify({
 reviewId: reviewId,
 fqAdviser: sent.fqAdviser,
 fqParaplanner: sent.fqParaplanner,
 aqAdviser: sent.aqAdviser,
 aqParaplanner: sent.aqParaplanner,
 fqContactId: sent.fqContactId,
 aqContactId: sent.aqContactId
 })
 };

 window.shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
 var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
 request.open('PATCH', '/_api/contacts({{ user.id }})', true);
 request.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
 request.setRequestHeader('__RequestVerificationToken', token);

 request.onreadystatechange = function () {
 if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }
 saving = false;

 if (request.status >= 200 && request.status < 300) {
 writeSavedAccountability({ at: Date.now(), state: sent });
 {% comment %}// Not "Saved" yet if something moved meanwhile: send it first.{% endcomment %}
 if (saveAgain) { saveAgain = false; save(); return; }
 var now = new Date();
 show('Saved ' + ('0' + now.getHours()).slice(-2) + ':'
 + ('0' + now.getMinutes()).slice(-2), 'success');
 return;
 }

 {% comment %}// A failed save is not retried: the error stays on screen, and the next change
 // sends the whole state again.{% endcomment %}
 saveAgain = false;
 var message = 'That could not be saved (' + request.status + ').';
 try {
 var parsed = JSON.parse(request.responseText);
 if (parsed && parsed.error && parsed.error.message) {
 message = parsed.error.message
 .replace('PRECONDITION: ', '').replace('VALIDATION: ', '').replace('UNAUTHORIZED: ', '');
 }
 } catch (e) { {% comment %}/* the status code is all there is */{% endcomment %} }
 show(message, 'error');
 };

 request.send(JSON.stringify(body));
 }).fail(function () {
 saving = false;
 show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
 });
 }

 function queue() {
 if (timer) { window.clearTimeout(timer); }
 timer = window.setTimeout(save, 700);
 }

 {% comment %}// Before anything is wired, so drawing the saved state is not itself a change to save.{% endcomment %}
 restoreSaved();
 reportAccountabilityLag();

 for (var i = 0; i < boxes.length; i++) { boxes[i].addEventListener('change', queue); }

 {% comment %}// change fires when a suggestion is picked; input covers typing the whole thing
 // out, which a datalist also allows.{% endcomment %}
 var people = root.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-acc-person]');
 for (var q = 0; q < people.length; q++) {
 people[q].addEventListener('change', queue);
 people[q].addEventListener('input', queue);
 }

 {% comment %}// The submit waits on this the way it waits on the header: a choice made a moment
 // before pressing Submit must reach the review before the outcome is created from it.{% endcomment %}
 {% comment %}/*
 * Shown and hidden as the answers change (2026-09-19). A non-pass anywhere on the
 * outcome scale means this check recorded a fail and somebody carries it.
 *
 * Bound to the questionnaire rather than to each answer's own save, because an
 * answer is saved on a debounce and the card should appear the moment the option
 * is ticked, not a second later.
 */{% endcomment %}
 var NON_PASS = ['120910301', '120910302', '120910303', '120910304'];

 function failed() {
 var ticked = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-questionnaire] input:checked');
 for (var i = 0; i < ticked.length; i++) {
 for (var n = 0; n < NON_PASS.length; n++) {
 if (ticked[i].value === NON_PASS[n]) { return true; }
 }
 }
 return false;
 }

 function refresh() {
 root.hidden = !failed();
 }

 var questionnaire = document.querySelector('[data-ot-questionnaire]');
 if (questionnaire) {
 questionnaire.addEventListener('change', refresh);
 }

 refresh();

 window.otAccountability = { flush: function (done) { save(); if (done) { done(true); } } };
 })();
 </script>
 {% endif %}

 {% if editable %}
 {% comment %}
 Fail points and remedial actions (project owner, 2026-09-29). The checker writes what
 the adviser is to do about each thing they marked down; the submit copies each one onto
 the remediation action it raises, and the adviser then says whether it was performed.

 Drawn by the script, not the Liquid: the rows are the fail points as they stand, and a
 tick autosaves without re-rendering the page, so a server-drawn list would be stale the
 moment the checker changed an answer (the same fault "Who carries this fail" had on
 IO-SEED-TAX-01). The list mirrors Remediation.NonPassItems; the server recomputes it at
 submit and refuses a missing row by name, so the mirror is a convenience, not the rule.

 Hidden until the check owes a remediation, and not rendered on a submitted review.
 {% endcomment %}
 <section class="ot-card ot-remedial"
 data-ot-remedial
 data-review-id="{{ rv.al_reviewinstanceid }}"
 data-review-kind="{% if is_tax_review %}tax{% else %}aqs{% endif %}"
 data-ot-tax-only="{% if rv['case.al_reviewrouteid'].name == 'Tax only' %}true{% endif %}"
 data-ot-remedial-saved="{{ rv.al_pendingremedialactions | escape }}"
 hidden
 aria-labelledby="ot-remedial-heading">
 <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-remedial-heading">Fail points and remedial actions</h2>
 <p>
 Each fail point below goes to the adviser with the remedial action you write for it.
 Write one for every row before you submit. The adviser answers whether it was performed.
 </p>
 <div class="ot-table-wrap">
 <table class="ot-table ot-remedial__table">
 <caption class="ot-visually-hidden">Remedial action for each fail point</caption>
 <thead>
 <tr>
 <th scope="col">No.</th>
 <th scope="col">Fail point</th>
 <th scope="col">Remedial action</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody data-ot-remedial-rows></tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 {% unless is_tax_review %}
 <div class="ot-field">
 <label for="ot-remedial-contact">Client contact required?</label>
 <select id="ot-remedial-contact" data-ot-remedial-contact>
 <option value="">Choose…</option>
 <option value="120910793">Yes</option>
 <option value="120910794">No</option>
 <option value="120910795">Potentially</option>
 </select>
 </div>
 {% endunless %}
 <p class="ot-accountability__status" data-ot-remedial-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 </section>

 <script>
 (function () {
 'use strict';
 var root = document.querySelector('[data-ot-remedial]');
 if (!root) { return; }

 var body = root.querySelector('[data-ot-remedial-rows]');
 var status = root.querySelector('[data-ot-remedial-status]');
 var reviewId = root.getAttribute('data-review-id');
 var isTax = root.getAttribute('data-review-kind') === 'tax';
 var OVERALL = '__overall__';

 /* ot-remedial-items:start */
 /*
 * The items the submit will raise, and whether it will raise any. Mirrors
 * Remediation.NonPassItems and SubmitReviewPlugin's remediation rules; executed by
 * portalRemedialActions.test.ts. Labels are al_response's own, not the page's: the
 * Tax grid prints 120910302 as "Pass with issues", the server writes "Insufficient
 * evidence", and the key has to be the server's.
 */
 function otRemedialItems(answers, failPoints, isTax) {
 var LABELS = { '120910301': 'Fail', '120910302': 'Insufficient evidence', '120910303': 'Pass with issues', '120910304': 'Potential harm', '120910306': 'No' };
 var CATEGORIES = { 'Q-TAX-05': true, 'Q-TAX-07': true, 'Q-TAX-09': true, 'Q-TAX-11': true };
 var OUTCOME = { 'Q-TAX-02': true, 'Q-FQ-01': true, 'Q-FQTAX-01': true };
 var SCALE = { '120910005': 'pf', '120910006': 'pf', '120910012': 'pf', '120910009': 'yni', '120910008': 'ynn' };

 function nonPass(type, value) {
 var scale = SCALE[type];
 if (!scale) { return false; }
 if (scale === 'ynn') { return value === '120910306'; }
 if (scale === 'yni') { return value === '120910306' || value === '120910302'; }
 if (type === '120910012' && value === '120910303') { return true; }
 return value === '120910301' || value === '120910302' || value === '120910304';
 }

 var items = [];
 var owed = false;
 var categories = 0;
 for (var i = 0; i < answers.length; i++) {
 var a = answers[i];
 var code = (a.code || '').toUpperCase();
 if (code === 'Q-FQ-03' || code === 'Q-FQTAX-03') {
 if (a.value === '120910305') { owed = true; }
 continue;
 }
 if (!isTax && code === 'Q-GR-01' && a.value && a.value !== '120910300') { owed = true; }
 if (isTax && code === 'Q-TAX-02' && (a.value === '120910301' || a.value === '120910302')) { owed = true; }
 if (isTax && CATEGORIES[code] && a.value === '120910305') { owed = true; categories += 1; }
 if (OUTCOME[code] || !a.value || !nonPass(a.type, a.value)) { continue; }
 var text = (a.text || '').trim();
 var word = a.type === '120910012' && a.value === '120910301' ? 'Potential harm' : LABELS[a.value];
 if (text) { items.push(text + ': ' + word); }
 }

 for (var f = 0; f < failPoints.length; f++) {
 var name = (failPoints[f] || '').trim();
 if (name) { items.push(name); }
 }

 return { owed: owed, items: items, categories: categories };
 }

 /*
 * What a check's answers allow its outcome questions to say (client decisions,
 * 2026-11-06, reversing "allow any answer"). Mirrors GradingRules.For; the server
 * refuses a submit that disagrees. Executed by portalRemedialActions.test.ts.
 */
 function otGrading(answers, failPoints) {
 var fqFail = failPoints.length > 0;
 var points = fqFail;
 var harm = false;
 var issues = false;
 var suitability = false;
 var grade = '';
 for (var i = 0; i < answers.length; i++) {
 var a = answers[i];
 var code = (a.code || '').toUpperCase();
 if (code === 'Q-GR-01') { grade = a.value; }
 if (!a.value) { continue; }
 if (code.indexOf('Q-AML') === 0) {
 points = true;
 if (a.value !== '120910305' && a.value !== '120910307') { fqFail = true; }
 } else if (a.type === '120910012') {
 suitability = true;
 if (a.value === '120910301' || a.value === '120910302' || a.value === '120910304') { harm = true; }
 if (a.value === '120910303') { issues = true; }
 }
 }
 var grades = null;
 if (suitability) {
 if (harm) { grades = ['120910302', '120910304']; }
 else if (issues) { grades = ['120910303']; }
 else if (fqFail) { grades = ['120910300', '120910303']; }
 else { grades = ['120910300']; }
 }
 if (grades && grades.length === 1) { grade = grades[0]; }
 return {
 fileQuality: points ? (fqFail ? '120910301' : '120910300') : null,
 grades: grades,
 remedial: fqFail || (grade !== '' && grade !== '120910300')
 };
 }
 /* ot-remedial-items:end */

 function answers() {
 var roots = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-answer]');
 var found = [];
 for (var i = 0; i < roots.length; i++) {
 var picked = roots[i].querySelector('input[type="radio"]:checked, input[type="checkbox"]:checked');
 var select = roots[i].querySelector('select');
 found.push({
 code: roots[i].getAttribute('data-question-code') || '',
 type: roots[i].getAttribute('data-response-type') || '',
 text: roots[i].getAttribute('data-question-text') || '',
 value: picked ? picked.value : (select ? select.value : '')
 });
 }
 return found;
 }

 function failPoints() {
 var ticked = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ot-failpoints-for] [data-ot-reason]:checked');
 var names = [];
 for (var i = 0; i < ticked.length; i++) {
 var label = document.querySelector('label[for="' + ticked[i].id + '"]');
 names.push(label ? label.textContent : '');
 }
 return names;
 }

 function show(message, kind) {
 status.textContent = message;
 status.className = 'ot-accountability__status' + (kind ? ' ot-inline-status--' + kind : '');
 }

 {% comment %}/*
 * Every text the checker has written on this review, drawn or not. A row that drops
 * out of the list keeps its words here, so unticking and re-ticking a fail point does
 * not lose them; the server ignores keys that are no longer items.
 */{% endcomment %}
 var texts = {};
 var saved = [];
 try {
 saved = JSON.parse(root.getAttribute('data-ot-remedial-saved') || '[]') || [];
 for (var s = 0; s < saved.length; s++) {
 if (saved[s] && saved[s].item) { texts[saved[s].item] = saved[s].text || ''; }
 }
 } catch (e) { texts = {}; saved = []; }

 /* ot-remedial-canonical:start */
 /*
 * A map as RemedialActionsRequestPlugin stores it - trimmed, blank entries dropped,
 * in key order - so what this tab sent and what the server later drew compare equal
 * whenever they say the same thing. Executed by portalRemedialActions.test.ts.
 */
 function canonical(entries) {
 var map = {};
 var keys = [];
 var list = entries || [];
 for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {
 var entry = list[i];
 if (!entry) { continue; }
 var key = String(entry.item || '').trim();
 var text = String(entry.text || '').trim();
 if (!key || !text) { continue; }
 if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(map, key)) { keys.push(key); }
 map[key] = text;
 }
 keys.sort();
 var pairs = [];
 for (var k = 0; k < keys.length; k++) { pairs.push([keys[k], map[keys[k]]]); }
 return JSON.stringify(pairs);
 }
 /* ot-remedial-canonical:end */

 {% comment %}// What the server sent, fixed at load: the thing a remembered save is compared to.{% endcomment %}
 var rendered = canonical(saved);

 {% comment %}/*
 * CACHE_LAG, as the header, the answers and "Who carries this fail" handle it. The
 * save goes through a plug-in that writes the review, so the site's render cache
 * learns of it late (AD-094: up to fifteen minutes) and a reload inside that window
 * draws the map from before the save - which the next save would then send over the
 * newer one, and a submit would stamp into the write-once al_remedialaction. The tab
 * remembers what it saved and says so; it never re-applies it, because words on
 * screen the server did not send cannot be told from words it did.
 */{% endcomment %}
 var REMEDIAL_LAG_KEY = 'ot.savedRemedial.' + reviewId;
 var REMEDIAL_LAG_WINDOW_MS = 20 * 60 * 1000;

 function readSavedRemedial() {
 try { return JSON.parse(window.sessionStorage.getItem(REMEDIAL_LAG_KEY) || 'null'); }
 catch (e) { return null; }
 }

 function writeSavedRemedial(remembered) {
 {% comment %}// Private browsing and a full store both throw; the notice is a courtesy.{% endcomment %}
 try {
 if (remembered === null) { window.sessionStorage.removeItem(REMEDIAL_LAG_KEY); }
 else { window.sessionStorage.setItem(REMEDIAL_LAG_KEY, JSON.stringify(remembered)); }
 } catch (e) { {% comment %}/* no notice this time */{% endcomment %} }
 }

 var current = [];
 var timer = null;
 var saving = false;
 var saveAgain = false;
 var waiting = [];
 var locked = false;

 function finish(ok) {
 var list = waiting;
 waiting = [];
 for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) { list[i](ok); }
 }

 function save(done) {
 if (done) { waiting.push(done); }
 if (timer) { window.clearTimeout(timer); timer = null; }
 if (saving) { saveAgain = true; return; }
 if (!window.shell || typeof window.shell.getTokenDeferred !== 'function') {
 show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
 finish(false);
 return;
 }

 var entries = [];
 for (var key in texts) {
 if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(texts, key) && (texts[key] || '').trim()) {
 entries.push({ item: key, text: texts[key] });
 }
 }
 {% comment %}// What this save sends, kept so a reload inside the cache window can be told apart
 // from one that has caught up (reportRemedialLag).{% endcomment %}
 var sent = entries;

 saving = true;
 show('Saving...', null);

 window.shell.getTokenDeferred().done(function (token) {
 var request = new XMLHttpRequest();
 request.open('PATCH', '/_api/contacts({{ user.id }})', true);
 request.setRequestHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
 request.setRequestHeader('__RequestVerificationToken', token);
 request.onreadystatechange = function () {
 if (request.readyState !== 4) { return; }
 saving = false;

 if (request.status >= 200 && request.status < 300) {
 writeSavedRemedial({ at: Date.now(), map: canonical(sent) });
 if (saveAgain) { saveAgain = false; save(null); return; }
 var now = new Date();
 show('Saved ' + ('0' + now.getHours()).slice(-2) + ':' + ('0' + now.getMinutes()).slice(-2), 'success');
 finish(true);
 return;
 }

 saveAgain = false;
 var message = 'Your remedial actions could not be saved (' + request.status + ').';
 try {
 var parsed = JSON.parse(request.responseText);
 if (parsed && parsed.error && parsed.error.message) {
 message = parsed.error.message
 .replace('PRECONDITION: ', '').replace('VALIDATION: ', '').replace('UNAUTHORIZED: ', '');
 }
 } catch (e) { {% comment %}/* the status code is all there is */{% endcomment %} }
 show(message, 'error');
 finish(false);
 };
 request.send(JSON.stringify({
 al_remedialactionsrequest: JSON.stringify({ reviewId: reviewId, actions: entries })
 }));
 }).fail(function () {
 saving = false;
 show('This page did not load completely. Refresh and try again.', 'error');
 finish(false);
 });
 }

 function queue() {
 if (timer) { window.clearTimeout(timer); }
 timer = window.setTimeout(function () { save(null); }, 700);
 }

 function onInput(event) {
 texts[event.target.getAttribute('data-ot-remedial-item')] = event.target.value;
 queue();
 }

 {% comment %}// Each further action on an item, by number: "item ##2" (RemedialActions.ExtraMark).{% endcomment %}
 function extras(key) {
 var stem = key + ' ##';
 var found = [];
 for (var k in texts) {
 if (texts[k] !== null && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(texts, k) && k.indexOf(stem) === 0 && /^\d+$/.test(k.slice(stem.length))) {
 found.push(k);
 }
 }
 found.sort(function (a, b) { return Number(a.slice(stem.length)) - Number(b.slice(stem.length)); });
 return found;
 }

 function withExtras(items) {
 var keys = [];
 for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) { keys = keys.concat([items[i]], extras(items[i])); }
 return keys;
 }

 function addExtra(key) {
 var list = extras(key);
 var last = list.length ? Number(list[list.length - 1].slice(key.length + 3)) : 1;
 texts[key + ' ##' + (last + 1)] = '';
 current = [];
 draw();
 }

 function removeExtra(key) {
 texts[key] = null;
 current = [];
 draw();
 queue();
 }

 function setAnswer(code, value) {
 var row = document.querySelector('[data-ot-answer][data-question-code="' + code + '"]');
 var input = row && row.querySelector('input[data-ot-input][value="' + value + '"]');
 if (!input || input.checked) { return; }
 input.checked = true;
 input.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true }));
 }

 function answerRow(code) {
 return document.querySelector('[data-ot-answer][data-question-code="' + code + '"]');
 }

 function hideRow(code, hide) {
 var row = answerRow(code);
 if (row) { row.hidden = hide; }
 return row;
 }

 function taxOnly() {
 var option = document.querySelector('select option[value="120910571"]');
 return root.getAttribute('data-ot-tax-only') === 'true' || (option && option.parentNode.value === '120910571');
 }

 {% comment %}// The Tax form: comments follow their Yes, and File Quality is AQS's unless Tax only.{% endcomment %}
 function syncTax(list, fails) {
 var pairs = [['Q-TAX-05', 'Q-TAX-06'], ['Q-TAX-07', 'Q-TAX-08'], ['Q-TAX-09', 'Q-TAX-10'], ['Q-TAX-11', 'Q-TAX-12']];
 var owed = fails.length > 0;
 for (var p = 0; p < pairs.length; p++) {
 var picked = answerRow(pairs[p][0]) && answerRow(pairs[p][0]).querySelector('input:checked');
 var yes = !!picked && picked.value === '120910305';
 owed = owed || yes;
 hideRow(pairs[p][1], !yes);
 }
 for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {
 if (list[i].code === 'Q-TAX-02' && (list[i].value === '120910301' || list[i].value === '120910302')) { owed = true; }
 }

 var alone = taxOnly();
 if (fails.length > 0 || !alone) { setAnswer('Q-FQTAX-01', fails.length > 0 ? '120910301' : '120910300'); }
 setAnswer('Q-FQTAX-03', owed ? '120910305' : '120910306');

 var codes = ['Q-FQTAX-01', 'Q-FQTAX-02', 'Q-FQTAX-03'];
 var table = null;
 for (var c = 0; c < codes.length; c++) {
 var row = hideRow(codes[c], !alone);
 if (row) { table = row.closest('table'); }
 }
 if (table) {
 table.hidden = !alone;
 var heading = table.previousElementSibling;
 if (heading && heading.tagName === 'H2') { heading.hidden = !alone; }
 }
 }

 function syncGrading(list, fails) {
 var rules = otGrading(list, fails);
 if (rules.fileQuality) { setAnswer('Q-FQ-01', rules.fileQuality); }

 var row = answerRow('Q-GR-01');
 var inputs = row ? row.querySelectorAll('input[data-ot-input]') : [];
 for (var i = 0; i < inputs.length; i++) {
 var barred = !!rules.grades && rules.grades.indexOf(inputs[i].value) < 0;
 inputs[i].disabled = barred;
 if (barred) { inputs[i].checked = false; }
 }
 if (rules.grades && rules.grades.length === 1) { setAnswer('Q-GR-01', rules.grades[0]); }

 setAnswer('Q-FQ-03', otGrading(answers(), fails).remedial ? '120910305' : '120910306');
 }

 function draw() {
 var list = answers();
 var fails = failPoints();
 if (!locked) {
 if (isTax) { syncTax(list, fails); } else { syncGrading(list, fails); }
 list = answers();
 }

 var result = otRemedialItems(list, fails, isTax);
 {% comment %}// Tax categories carry their own words, so only a check with nothing else needs the card.{% endcomment %}
 root.hidden = !result.owed || (result.categories > 0 && result.items.length === 0);

 var keys = withExtras(result.items.length ? result.items : [OVERALL]);
 if (keys.join('\n') === current.join('\n')) { return; }
 current = keys;

 while (body.firstChild) { body.removeChild(body.firstChild); }
 for (var i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {
 var row = document.createElement('tr');
 var number = document.createElement('td');
 number.textContent = String(i + 1);
 var label = document.createElement('td');
 var further = / ##\d+$/.test(keys[i]);
 var stem = keys[i].replace(/ ##\d+$/, '');
 label.textContent = (stem === OVERALL ? 'Overall' : stem) + (further ? ' (further action)' : '');
 var cell = document.createElement('td');
 var box = document.createElement('textarea');
 box.rows = 3;
 box.maxLength = 4000;
 box.required = true;
 box.className = 'ot-response-cell__text';
 box.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Remedial action for ' + (keys[i] === OVERALL ? 'this check' : keys[i]));
 box.setAttribute('data-ot-remedial-item', keys[i]);
 box.value = texts[keys[i]] || '';
 {% comment %}// A redraw after submit must not hand back a live box (lock).{% endcomment %}
 box.disabled = locked;
 box.addEventListener('input', onInput);
 box.addEventListener('blur', function () { save(null); });
 cell.appendChild(box);

 {% comment %}// One query per box: another action on this item raises its own remediation row.{% endcomment %}
 var more = document.createElement('button');
 more.type = 'button';
 more.className = 'ot-btn';
 more.textContent = further ? 'Remove this action' : 'Add another remedial action';
 more.disabled = locked;
 more.addEventListener('click', (function (key, isExtra) {
 return function () { if (isExtra) { removeExtra(key); } else { addExtra(key); } };
 })(keys[i], further));
 cell.appendChild(more);
 row.appendChild(number);
 row.appendChild(label);
 row.appendChild(cell);
 body.appendChild(row);
 }
 }

 function missing() {
 if (root.hidden) { return null; }
 for (var i = 0; i < current.length; i++) {
 if (!(texts[current[i]] || '').trim()) {
 return current[i] === OVERALL
 ? 'Write the overall remedial action under "Fail points and remedial actions" before submitting.'
 : 'Write the remedial action for "' + current[i].replace(/ ##\d+$/, '') + '" before submitting.';
 }
 }
 if (contact && !contact.value) {
 return 'Answer "Client contact required?" under "Fail points and remedial actions" before submitting.';
 }
 return null;
 }

 {% comment %}// The AQS checker's answer, parked with the words and written onto each action raised.{% endcomment %}
 var contact = root.querySelector('[data-ot-remedial-contact]');
 if (contact) {
 contact.value = texts.__clientcontact__ || '';
 contact.addEventListener('change', function () {
 texts.__clientcontact__ = contact.value;
 save(null);
 });
 }

 function reportRemedialLag() {
 var remembered = readSavedRemedial();
 if (!remembered || typeof remembered.at !== 'number') { return; }
 if (Date.now() - remembered.at > REMEDIAL_LAG_WINDOW_MS || remembered.map === rendered) {
 writeSavedRemedial(null);
 return;
 }
 show('Your remedial actions are not shown here yet. Your last change was saved. This'
 + ' site caches pages for up to fifteen minutes, so a reload can arrive before the'
 + ' page catches up. Do not change them again yet — reload in a few minutes, or'
 + ' the next change would save what is on screen over it.', 'error');
 }

 {% comment %}/*
 * The review has been submitted (lockPage). The card sits outside the questionnaire,
 * so the page's own lock does not reach it: its boxes are disabled here and a save
 * still in its debounce is dropped - the server would refuse it for a submitted check.
 */{% endcomment %}
 function lock() {
 locked = true;
 if (timer) { window.clearTimeout(timer); timer = null; }
 var boxes = root.querySelectorAll('textarea, select, button');
 for (var b = 0; b < boxes.length; b++) { boxes[b].disabled = true; }
 }

 {% comment %}// Any change outside the card may move the list: an answer, a fail point tick.{% endcomment %}
 document.addEventListener('change', function (event) {
 if (event.target && !root.contains(event.target)) { draw(); }
 });

 draw();
 reportRemedialLag();

 window.otRemedial = {
 missing: missing,
 redraw: draw,
 lock: lock,
 flush: function (done) {
 if (root.hidden) { done(true); return; }
 save(done);
 }
 };
 })();
 </script>
 {% endif %}

 {% unless editable %}
 {% comment %}
 The remedial actions this check raised, read-only (project owner, 2026-10-05: add the
 remediation actions to the PDF downloaded from the portal). The editable card above is
 not rendered once the review is submitted, so without this the page and its Save as
 PDF lost them. CheckRemedialActions draws the same table into the emailed document.

 The fail points are split out of al_description as OT Case Detail splits them:
 newline_to_br then a one-character split, and a line is a fail point when putting
 "- " back in front of it with its first "- " removed reproduces it.

 Each cell's text is stripped before its fallback: default only falls back on null or
 an empty string, and the server treats text that is only spaces as empty
 (IsNullOrWhiteSpace), so a row of spaces would otherwise print as a blank cell here
 and as the fallback in the emailed document.

 Row order: CheckRemedialActions.Actions (plugins/OutcomeTesting.Plugins/
 CheckRemedialActions.cs) sorts by createdon, then by the numeric index after
 al_remediationactioncode's last '-' (codes read "REM-<caseref>-<seq>" for a lone
 action, "REM-<caseref>-<seq>-<index>" when itemised; a case reference may itself
 contain dashes, which is why only the LAST '-' counts). createdon commonly ties
 across ten or more rows raised in one transaction, so the fetch's own order reads
 1, 10, 2, 3... once a check has ten actions. The fix here does not re-sort a list
 (this Liquid has no sort filter): it walks the band of possible index values
 1..(count + 1) and, on each pass, emits whichever action's own index matches that
 pass's number. The last pass (count + 1) is a catch-all for an index that matched
 none of 1..count, so a bad or missing code still renders exactly once instead of
 vanishing.

 The index is never converted to a number: this site runs DotLiquid, whose plus
 filter concatenates when its input is a string instead of adding (the string "3"
 run through plus: 0 is string.Concat, giving "30", not 3). rr_tail stays a string
 straight out of the split, and the pass number is captured into a string of its own
 (rr_n, rr_k) so the comparison is string equals string throughout; rr_size, n and k
 themselves are genuine integers (from .size and a Liquid range), so the range and
 the rr_last addition below are unaffected by this and stay numeric.
 {% endcomment %}
 {% fetchxml review_actions %}
 <fetch>
 <entity name="al_remediationaction">
 <attribute name="al_remediationactionid" />
 <attribute name="al_description" />
 <attribute name="al_remedialaction" />
 <attribute name="al_adviserresponse" />
 <attribute name="al_assignedcontactid" />
 <attribute name="al_duedate" />
 <attribute name="al_actionstatus" />
 <attribute name="al_remediationactioncode" />
 <attribute name="createdon" />
 <filter type="and">
 <condition attribute="al_reviewinstanceid" operator="eq" value="{{ review_id | xml_escape }}" />
 <condition attribute="statecode" operator="eq" value="0" />
 </filter>
 <order attribute="createdon" descending="false" />
 <order attribute="al_remediationactioncode" descending="false" />
 </entity>
 </fetch>
 {% endfetchxml %}
 {% assign review_actions_list = review_actions.results.entities %}
 {% if review_actions_list.size > 0 %}
 <section class="ot-card ot-remedial" data-ot-remedial-read aria-labelledby="ot-remedial-read-heading">
 <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-remedial-read-heading">Remedial actions</h2>
 <div class="ot-table-wrap">
 <table class="ot-table ot-remedial__table">
 <thead>
 <tr>
 <th scope="col">No.</th>
 <th scope="col">Fail point</th>
 <th scope="col">Remedial action</th>
 <th scope="col">Owner</th>
 <th scope="col">Target date</th>
 <th scope="col">Status</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody>
 {% assign rr_no = 0 %}
 {% assign rr_size = review_actions_list.size %}
 {% assign rr_last = rr_size | plus: 1 %}
 {% for n in (1..rr_last) %}
 {% for a in review_actions_list %}
 {% assign rr_parts = a.al_remediationactioncode | default: '' | split: '-' %}
 {% assign rr_tail = '' %}
 {% for s in rr_parts %}{% assign rr_tail = s %}{% endfor %}
 {% assign rr_show = false %}
 {% if rr_size == 1 %}
 {% if n == 1 %}{% assign rr_show = true %}{% endif %}
 {% else %}
 {% if n < rr_last %}
 {% capture rr_n %}{{ n }}{% endcapture %}
 {% if rr_tail == rr_n %}{% assign rr_show = true %}{% endif %}
 {% else %}
 {% assign rr_in_range = false %}
 {% for k in (1..rr_size) %}
 {% capture rr_k %}{{ k }}{% endcapture %}
 {% if rr_tail == rr_k %}{% assign rr_in_range = true %}{% endif %}
 {% endfor %}
 {% unless rr_in_range %}{% assign rr_show = true %}{% endunless %}
 {% endif %}
 {% endif %}
 {% if rr_show %}
 {% assign rr_checker = a.al_remedialaction | strip %}
 {% assign rr_adviser = a.al_adviserresponse | strip %}
 {% assign rr_text = rr_checker | default: rr_adviser | default: '—' %}
 {% assign rr_owner = a.al_assignedcontactid.name | strip | default: 'Nobody assigned' %}
 {% assign rr_due = '—' %}{% if a.al_duedate %}{% assign rr_due = a.al_duedate | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' %}{% endif %}
 {% assign rr_status = a.al_actionstatus.label | strip | default: '—' %}
 {% assign rr_flat = a.al_description | default: '' | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', '|' | replace: '<br>', '|' %}
 {% assign rr_lines = rr_flat | split: '|' %}
 {% assign rr_count = 0 %}
 {% for l in rr_lines %}{% assign line = l | strip %}{% assign rest = line | remove_first: '- ' %}{% assign rebuilt = '- ' | append: rest %}{% if rebuilt == line %}{% assign rr_count = rr_count | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
 {% if rr_count == 0 %}
 {% assign rr_no = rr_no | plus: 1 %}
 <tr>
 <td>{{ rr_no }}</td>
 <td>—</td>
 <td>{{ rr_text | escape | newline_to_br }}</td>
 <td>{{ rr_owner | escape }}</td>
 <td>{{ rr_due }}</td>
 <td>{{ rr_status | escape }}</td>
 </tr>
 {% else %}
 {% assign rr_shown = 0 %}
 {% for l in rr_lines %}
 {% assign line = l | strip %}{% assign rest = line | remove_first: '- ' %}{% assign rebuilt = '- ' | append: rest %}
 {% if rebuilt == line %}
 {% assign rr_shown = rr_shown | plus: 1 %}
 {% assign rr_no = rr_no | plus: 1 %}
 <tr>
 <td>{{ rr_no }}</td>
 <td>{{ rest | escape }}</td>
 {% if rr_shown == 1 %}
 <td rowspan="{{ rr_count }}">{{ rr_text | escape | newline_to_br }}</td>
 <td rowspan="{{ rr_count }}">{{ rr_owner | escape }}</td>
 <td rowspan="{{ rr_count }}">{{ rr_due }}</td>
 <td rowspan="{{ rr_count }}">{{ rr_status | escape }}</td>
 {% endif %}
 </tr>
 {% endif %}
 {% endfor %}
 {% endif %}
 {% endif %}
 {% endfor %}
 {% endfor %}
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 </section>
 {% endif %}
 {% comment %}
 A Tax check with AQS still to come raises nothing until the AQS submit, so its words are
 still parked on the review. Liquid here cannot read JSON, so the script draws them. No
 email goes at this stage, so this page is the only place they can be seen or saved.
 {% endcomment %}
 {% if review_actions_list.size == 0 and rv.al_pendingremedialactions %}
 <section class="ot-card ot-remedial" data-ot-remedial-parked="{{ rv.al_pendingremedialactions | escape }}" aria-labelledby="ot-remedial-parked-heading">
 <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-remedial-parked-heading">Remedial actions</h2>
 <p>These go to the adviser once the AQS check is submitted.</p>
